        "path": "correction-1193-v1/root/proposed-v2/Sludge_fluid.yaml",
        "sha256": "7ba71cdaf547a4a72c2210c1174f5a9c095def40399d8486e02df9c4f0ca9468"
      },
      "removed_new_resolving_aliases": [
        "Sludge fluid (medium 119)"
      ],
      "correction": "The existing Sludge_fluid owner spans source-described liquid material from sludge. Its MICRO0000521 exact target asserts municipal origin, while DSMZ119/JCM872 specify anaerobic-digester sludge without that origin. TOGO M2596 separately identifies Ithaca wastewater sludge and its own clarification process. Reuse this existing generic material owner with a local registry identity rather than duplicate it or force municipal origin on every source. The DSMZ119/JCM872 yeast-incubated supernatant is a distinct supplied preparation; the M2596 input and further SS preparation must retain their own source-qualified processing and must not receive the119 formula."
    },
